      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Council approved the Development Review Permit, Special Design Permit, removal of 26 Heritage trees, and a Vesting Tentative Map (Resolution No. 18972) creating 22 residential lots and five common lots, replacing a vacant home, a vacant private school and a commercial building.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003847",
        "SRC-003850"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Council report lists home sizes of about 2,900 to 4,900 sq ft. The developer site lists 2,413 to 3,729 sq ft, 4 to 5 bedrooms, and prices from the $3 millions.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003847",
        "SRC-003849"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The May 2026 final map report says a second driveway onto Moorpark Way was added after approval. It also says the developer paid $328,985 in subdivision fees and deferred about $1,248,400 in impact fees until occupancy under SB 937.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003850"
      ]
    }
